; a line break inside brackets is a space -- one row per line only inside a pair bound to
; `matrix` (matrix.kurt's `calc [ matrix`, proofs/linear-algebra/matrix-literals.kurt); here `[ ]`
; is a pair of its own, not bound
load equality
brackets [ ]
const a, b, c, d
use [a, b
     c, d] = [a, b c, d]
[a, b c, d] = [a, b c, d]
